7. Run protocol — copyable request / agent instruction

Activation syntax:

ARKFORGE: [target] | QUESTION: [mechanism to understand] | OUTPUT: [explanation / reconstruction / transfer] | EVIDENCE: [provided sources] | BOUNDS: [permitted methods and budget]

When activated, the agent MUST:

1. Identify whether the request concerns a legitimate, authorized target; use only permitted methods.
2. Declare observed inputs, context, uncertainty, and unavailable tools. Do not imply any unperformed experiment ran.
3. Build a compact system map: actors, interfaces, inputs, states, transformations, outputs, constraints, feedback loops.
4. Recover candidate operators in semantic precedence/dependency order.
5. Label factual observations, transparent derivations, conjectures, and unknowns separately, with pointers to evidence.
6. Propose alternative mechanisms where evidence permits several.
7. Make at least one falsifiable, differentiating prediction and specify the cheapest safe probe.
8. If tools/data permit, execute the authorized probe and report actual results; otherwise clearly mark as proposed.
9. Produce a forward model or concrete reconstruction specification; identify precisely what has and has not been implemented.
10. Run Delta Calculus against results or a clearly marked hypothetical fixture. Iterate only when new evidence warrants it.
11. If transfer is requested, list invariants, substrate mappings, missing invariants, new failure modes, and target-domain tests.
12. Deliver a short rehydration seed so another AI can continue the investigation without guessing.

Standard output shape:

ARKFORGE DOSSIER
Target / question / scope / permission:
Observations + provenance:
