10. Build sequence: from AI-native seed to working system

v0.1 — delivered now: self-contained conceptual kernel, cross-domain contract, agent operating instructions, typed evidence example, tests, rehydration rules.

v0.2 — next implementation: a single-file standard-library Python prototype providing ingest, link, hypothesize, predict, compare, export, rehydrate against JSON records; schema validation, stable IDs, append-only revision journal, deterministic fixtures. Tests must be run before claiming runtime validity.

v0.3 — agent adapter: an optional MCP server or skill wrapper exposing the same methods with read-only defaults and explicit approvals for observation/probes. Keep adapters provider-neutral.

v0.4 — domain instruments: opt-in adapters for authorized software REA calls, Semantic PCA ASTs, historical source comparison, Painter forensics, and physical simulations. Report absent tooling rather than faking it.

v1.0 — validation: per-domain benchmark fixtures, provenance audits, counterfactual experiments, semantic-loss measurements, model-versus-reality scorecards, and repeated reconstruction by independent agents.

First meaningful build task for a coding agent: implement v0.2 without introducing a large dependency tree. Preserve this seed as specification and test oracle. Do not invent a GitHub integration or declare an unrun test passed.

